3. FIRST-PARTY COMPONENTS, KERNEL MODULE (GPL) & THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
================================================================================

3.1 First-Party & Adapted Native Android Binaries (`panel/realme-bengal/bin/`):
All custom C system utilities and daemons located under `panel/realme-bengal/bin/` 
— specifically `amp-status`, `aplay`, `audio-test`, `clear`, `esputil`, 
`jacktor-api`, `jacktor-motd`, `otg-trigger`, and `serial-bridge` — are original 
works or adaptations authored and copyrighted by Ardo Zapp:
  Copyright (c) 2026 Ardo Zapp
  License: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

(The sole third-party binary inside `panel/realme-bengal/bin/` is `socat/`, which is a 
third-party open-source utility governed by the GNU General Public License v2.0 
as detailed in Section 3.4 below.)

3.2 First-Party Kernel Driver (`usb-serial.kpm` — GPL-2.0-or-later):
The Universal USB-to-Serial KernelPatch Module driver located at:
  panel/realme-bengal/kpm/usb-serial/
is an original work authored and copyrighted by Ardo Zapp:
  Copyright (c) 2026 Ardo Zapp

Because this driver executes inside Linux kernel space and interfaces directly 
with Linux kernel symbols, TTY core subsystems, and USB host APIs, it is 
specifically licensed under the:
  GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)
This ensures strict compliance with Linux kernel GPL licensing and prevents any 
licensing violations or symbol linkage conflicts with the upstream Linux kernel.

3.3 Custom Linux Kernel 4.19 Adaptation & Pre-Patched Partition Images:
The adapted Linux Kernel (`4.19.152-perf+`) authored and compiled by Ardo Zapp 
for the Realme C15 Qualcomm Bengal platform (`panel/realme-bengal/image/boot.img.xz`), 
along with any corresponding kernel patches, is distributed in strict compliance 
with the:
  GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPL-2.0-only)

3.4 Third-Party Components & Bundled Open-Source Software:
The Jacktor Audio repository bundles or links against third-party open-source 
components and libraries. These components are NOT covered by CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 
and remain subject to their respective original copyright holders and licenses:

- esputil Base Origin Notice (`panel/realme-bengal/bin/esputil/`):
  Contains portions derived from cpq/esputil (https://github.com/cpq/esputil), 
  Copyright (c) 2021-2023 Cesanta Software Limited, licensed under the MIT License. 
  In accordance with the permissive sublicensing rights of the MIT License, all 
  subsequent modifications, AArch64 Musl porting, and Jacktor Audio ecosystem 
  integrations authored by Ardo Zapp are licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
- socat Base Origin & Porting Notice (`panel/realme-bengal/bin/socat/` and bundled binary 
  in `panel/realme-bengal/modul/jacktor-audio-framework/system/bin/socat`):
  Originally authored by Gerhard Rieger and contributors (http://www.dest-unreach.org/socat/).
  Subject to the GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPL-2.0-only).
  Ported and adapted to standalone AArch64 Musl static build for Android by Ardo Zapp in 
  full compliance with GPL-2.0-only. Complete source code and build Makefile are maintained in 
  `panel/realme-bengal/bin/socat/`. The standalone `serial-bridge` daemon executes `socat` as 
  an independent subprocess via `fork()`/`exec()` and does not link against `socat` libraries.
- BusyBox NDK (`panel/realme-bengal/modul/jacktor-audio-framework/system/bin/busybox`):
  Copyright (c) Erik Andersen, Rob Landley, Denys Vlasenko, and contributors.
  Subject to the GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPL-2.0-only).
- KissFFT Real-to-Complex Transform Engine (`firmware/amplifier/include/driver/kissfft`):
  Copyright (c) Mark Borgerding. Subject to the 3-Clause BSD License.
- cJSON Library (`firmware/amplifier/managed_components`):
  Copyright (c) Dave Gamble and cJSON contributors. Subject to the MIT License.
- esp-idf-lib Drivers (DS3231, ADS1115, i2cdev, esp_idf_lib_helpers):
  Copyright (c) Ruslan V. Uss and contributors. Subject to the MIT / BSD-3-Clause License.
- Espressif Drivers (`onewire_bus`, `ds18b20`):
  Copyright (c) Espressif Systems. Subject to the Apache License 2.0.
- Android Audio Policy Configuration (`panel/realme-bengal/modul/jacktor-audio-framework`):
  Subject to the Apache License 2.0.
- JetBrains Mono & Inter Fonts (`panel/realme-bengal/modul/jacktor-audio-framework/webroot/webfonts`):
  Copyright (c) JetBrains s.r.o. and Rasmus Andersson.
  Subject to the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1).
- Font Awesome Free Web Assets (`panel/realme-bengal/modul/jacktor-audio-framework/webroot`):
  Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License.

